Ray and Edward are right that the ideology of Star Trek is hostile to
our ideas. 

I've _always_ thought Roddenberry's universe was crummy. I was around
13-14 or so when the show first aired (yes, the "Star Trek: The
Original Generation"). I'd been reading a lot of Heinlein, and was
about to get into Rand, so the oh-so-correct philosophy of the "Prime
Directive" and "Things Man was Not Meant to Know" were kind of
disgusting. The peace and brotherhood nonsense also bothered me (after
all, some folks--and some aliens--just plain _need_ killing).

