(My reaction to the special effects in "Star Wars" was even greater
than my reaction to "2001"...I'd seen the sets and some of the actors
at the 1976 WorldCon, but was still totally unprepared for the
magnitude of the effects, beginning with the ship moving overhead
across the screen--and getting bigger and bigger as the Dolby sound
system kicked in. The minor errors (explosions and sound in space)
didn't bother me. Nor did the pseudo-Zen of "The Force.")

I caught the only episode of "Babylon Five" a while back. It may have
promise. No greedy "Ferengi" capitalistic pigs, no "Federation"
Gestapo to make sure Man is not going where he is forbidden to go....

We'll see. I still don't have cable, so reception is problematic.

