they're saying, "You could be immortal, and powerful, and beautiful
forever, but YOU WOULDN'T LIKE IT". I'd rather find out for myself
whether I like it. 

The most sensible portrayal of immortality that I've seen in sf
was *The Golden Space* by Pamela Sargeant. (I think I've got the
right author/title.) After immortality, a few people commit suicide
and a few go mad, but most figure out how to handle it.

In fact, we don't even know what 150 or 200 year olds would be like.
There may be sorts of maturity we're not familar with.

Any *Back to Methuselah* fans here?

Just to be fair to Star Trek, they do have the problem of aging actors,
which leaves out having a longevity technology on the show, unless
you assume that it's easy to duplicate but hard to edit, so that
people only rejuvenate when they have to, and come back a little
different (and can be played by younger but similar looking actors
or actresses).

